    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Liam Hicks** stands out as our primary offensive engine, carrying an efficiency score of 53.01. Batting out of the #3 hole against Armstrong, **Hicks** benefits from a favorable 4.35 xERA matchup and a significant +11% dynamic platoon edge, positioning him as our most reliable asset to generate counting stats. While **Brayan Rocchio** also makes the active roster, his 43.06 score reflects the heavy penalty of batting ninth against Peralta, F; he remains a marginal start strictly due to the lack of alternatives in our current pool, serving as a placeholder while we await the return of our core stars.\n\nThe bench remains heavily populated by our marquee talent, as **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** are all inactive due to scheduled team off-days, effectively paralyzing our offensive ceiling. Furthermore, the absence of **Luis Robert Jr.**\u2014still sidelined on the IL\u2014remains a critical blow to our stolen base production, leaving us devoid of elite speed options for this rotation. Among the reserves, **Heliot Ramos** and **Jackson Merrill** were the closest to cracking the lineup, but were ultimately benched to preserve our remaining game caps in anticipation of more favorable matchups later in the week. We are closely monitoring weather reports for the stadium, though no immediate risks have been flagged that would necessitate pulling **Hicks** or **Rocchio** before first pitch.",
